{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794606444,"nonce":"4zqMRy05ff/lfNgiei4gVsHolSQ=","title":"A complex Field's Dirichlet constraint written with bind is refused as not affine","message":"For a complex unknown (fem_symbols(..., complex=True)), u.bind(x=xb, y=yb) - g on a boundary gives a ComplexPair whose real and imaginary parts are refused by jno.fem: 'an essential boundary/initial condition must be affine in the unknown ... Got: (TrialFunction(u_re, value_shape=()) - Literal(0.0))'; with the pair left as [c.real, c.imag] the imaginary part fails in _build_dirichlet_pairs with 'Cannot evaluate: \u003cclass float\u003e'. The same constraint on a real unknown, u.bind(x=xb, y=yb) - g, works, and so does u.real(xb, yb) - jnp.real(g), u.imag(xb, yb) - jnp.imag(g). Expected: ComplexPair.bind on a boundary gives the same constraint as calling each part at the boundary coordinates.","files":null}]}